# Project Veil: this emsdk is committed on purpose, trimmed to what the SpacetimeDB
# wasm module build (spacetime/veil_world) needs. Windows x64 only.
#
# Removed as not needed for that build, so these do NOT work here: emcc --closure
# and the Babel / html-minifier node_modules, emrun, -sWASM=0 (wasm2js), the
# wasm32-*clang copies, lld.exe (wasm-ld.exe is kept), the LLVM analysis tools,
# Python's pip / pywin32 / psutil, npm, and emscripten's own tests and docs.
# For any of that, use a full emsdk (emsdk install / activate) in another folder.
#
# Upstream emsdk ignores /upstream, /node, /python and /.emscripten because it
# downloads them; here they ARE the dependency, so they are tracked. The root
# .gitignore ignores *.exe and *.a, and a nested file wins over its parent, so
# they are re-included below.
!*.exe
!*.a
!*.o
# ...and the root's folder / file rules that hit emscripten's own sources:
# upstream/emscripten/tools/ (emcc's Python modules), docs/, Makefile
!tools/
!docs/
!Makefile

*.pyc
__pycache__

# Regenerated by emcc on the first build (system libraries compiled for wasm32)
/upstream/emscripten/cache/

# Tags files that get generated at runtime
/emscripten-releases-tot.txt
/.emscripten.old
/.emscripten_cache
/.emscripten_cache__last_clear
/.emscripten_sanity
/.emscripten_sanity_wasm

# Other things emsdk can download that this build does not use
/ccache
/gnu
/fastcomp
/fastcomp-clang/
/llvm
/ninja
/releases
/clang
/emscripten
/git
/temp
/crunch
/java
/mingw
/spidermonkey
/binaryen
/firefox
/cmake
